      </entryLinks>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Wyrdboy" id="3044-e034-0aad-1bf4" hidden="false" targetId="2196-8f4c-05a5-b2dc" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Independent Character" id="0a47-cb2b-e6e8-4cbc" hidden="false" targetId="4a60-7f7e-c37f-a4d6" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Psychic Vomit" id="41fc-7a13-741f-e2ad" hidden="false" page="11" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
          <description>Unable to contain the Ork energies any longer the Wyrdboy vents ti forth in a stream of green psychogenic energy. Place the flamer template with the narrow end touching the Wyrdboy. Each model even partially under the template suffers an automatic Strength 4 hit.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Gork&apos;ll Get &apos;Em" id="f348-9719-0672-e118" hidden="false" page="11" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
          <description>The Wyrdboy&apos;s belief in Mork and Gork is so complete that it causes a manifestation of their power. This takes the form of a large green fist or foot descending from above. This counts as a shooting attack. The Ork Wyrdboy must be able to see his target, and rolls to hit as normal.

Range 72&quot;
Strength 8
AP -
Assault 1, Blast</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Minor Psychic Power" id="fd28-ca47-2f2a-b17e" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
          <costs>
